# How to cite shrink-array. GitHub reads this file ("Cite this repository").
# No version here on purpose: cite the release you used (its tag).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use shrink-array in work you publish, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "shrink-array: compressed chunk arrays for C++ HPC codes"
abstract: >-
  Arrays for C++ HPC codes that are used like a std::vector and take less
  memory when large parts of them hold the same value. An array is cut into
  chunks; a chunk whose elements are all equal keeps no buffer of its own.
  Arrays of a billion elements, written concurrently from OpenMP threads,
  std::threads or TBB tasks, with no lock on the write path.
authors:
  - family-names: Ballereau
    given-names: Philippe
    affiliation: "CEA"
repository-code: "https://github.com/cea-hpc/shrink-array"
url: "https://github.com/cea-hpc/shrink-array"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - HPC
  - C++20
  - compressed arrays
  - sparse data
  - memory footprint
  - OpenMP
  - lock-free
